0370e868ffe3b1569a4b10af8","length":"1805.3","height":"0","width":"0"},{"name":"radia_s07_n059_RadioCult.png","source":"derivative","format":"PNG","original":"radia_s07_n059_RadioCult.mp3","mtime":"1493159335","size":"10985","md5":"28a485edfa6b16cccd146fb699993157","crc32":"0206a232","sha1":"8fd24848491a9a8ca299aafb4259b801b7cb0fa2"},{"name":"radia_s07_n059_RadioCult_archive.torrent","source":"metadata","btih":"3a6f94583718814297f526e0ca873aa03fce981a","mtime":"1555130786","size":"4678","md5":"3c23f52ff465c973ee79c8a3757cd637","crc32":"5242dcff","sha1":"62020206440e6c5f200130e1b8f5c342176b311f","format":"Archive BitTorrent"},{"name":"radia_s07_n059_RadioCult_files.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","md5":"65f2f64f716d350c4533c82bd58523e5","summation":"md5"},{"name":"radia_s07_n059_RadioCult_meta.sqlite","source":"original","mtime":"1493159243","size":"18432","format":"Metadata","md5":"c22ba5dc3af763747ed840c05770b9b4","crc32":"62e3ff7d","sha1":"10496ec9e83caaee45dcd82b7306b0ba15e33102"},{"name":"radia_s07_n059_RadioCult_meta.xml","source":"metadata","mtime":"1669138801","size":"2004","format":"Metadata","md5":"a3ea21e1226ac4434fc6d87bbf9f43e6","crc32":"0b1ed278","sha1":"e807cddfb0abe377fea8ba19c9642627b40af6ed"}],"files_count":11,"item_last_updated":1669138801,"item_size":48837003,"metadata":{"identifier":"radia_s07_n059_RadioCult","mediatype":"audio","collection":["radiafm","radioprograms","radiostationarchives"],"creator":"Radio Cult","date":"2006-05-15","description":"Hello… this is Not That Kyd from Radio Cult and you are \nlistening to Radia Emission number 59. Renee Sills sometimes performs \nunder the moniker Miss Matches. She took on the courageous task of \ncreating one full radia lenght piece and it turned out greater than the \ngreat Canadian Mountains. The piece goes up and down with ever changing \nlandscape like the jagged mountains do too. For any of you who have \nnever been to Montreal, well this show also look at lot like there.<br /><div class=\"entry-content\"><p>\nThe samples in Renees mix come from a billion local and not so local \nartists… Charles Stankievitch, Frieda Abtan, Lateef, Serviceworks, Josh \nIvy, some children and way more. Renee’s mashup style is always present \nboth in her audio and video works. She is interested in exploring the \npossibilities available for sharing within a radio network and this is \napparent sonically throught this piece. Again this is Renee Sills. She’s\n from Colorado, she lives in Montreal, she owns an accordeon and she \nwant to visit Bulgaria.</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>","licenseurl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0/","radiaseason":"7","scanner":"Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.6.3","subject":"radio art;Radia;Radio Cult","title":"Show 0059: Renee Sills (Radio Cult)","publicdate":"2017-04-25 22:26:47","uploader":"radia.fm@gmail.com","addeddate":"2017-04-25 22:26:47","year":"2006","backup_location":"ia906402_34","external_metadata_update":"2019-04-13T04:46:15Z"},"server":"ia801509.us.archive.org","uniq":1288263628,"workable_servers":["ia801509.us.archive.org","ia601509.us.archive.org"]}